From 04925c612e27186f340587cf8c097adec33a20e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjorn Pagen <bjorn.pagen@alpha.school>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 10:54:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fixincludes: darwin sys/_types/_rsize_t.h breaks under GCC
 -fmodules

The macOS SDK's <sys/_types/_rsize_t.h> gates its clang-modules branch
on __has_feature(modules), assuming that any compiler reporting the
modules feature is clang and implements clang's stddef.h __need_rsize_t
protocol.  GCC also reports __has_feature(modules) under -fmodules, but
its stddef.h does not implement that protocol, so rsize_t is never
defined and the C11 Annex K declarations in the SDK's <_string.h> fail
to parse:

_string.h:176:48: error: 'rsize_t' has not been declared

In particular this breaks the libstdc++ std module build on darwin.
Rewrite the guard to require __clang__ so that GCC always takes the
SDK's plain-typedef branch.

fixincludes/ChangeLog:

	* inclhack.def (darwin_rsize_t_modules): New fix.
	* fixincl.x: Regenerate.
	* tests/base/sys/_types/_rsize_t.h: New test.

Signed-off-by: Bjorn Pagen <bjorn.pagen@alpha.school>
---
 fixincludes/fixincl.x                        | 56 ++++++++++++++++++--
 fixincludes/inclhack.def                     | 25 +++++++++
 fixincludes/tests/base/sys/_types/_rsize_t.h | 18 +++++++
 3 files changed, 96 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 fixincludes/tests/base/sys/_types/_rsize_t.h

